  "goodToKnow": "Der Tabak is tobacco: Tabak rauchen, Pfeifentabak, Tabakwaren. Das ist starker Tabak means that's a bit much or that's outrageous, said about a cheeky claim. In Germany, it's stressed on the first syllable (TA-bak), while Austrians say ta-BAK. In Austria, tobacco and newspapers are sold at a Trafik. Germany was long known as a smokers' country with cigarette machines on the street, but smoking rates and rules have tightened, with Nichtraucherschutz laws in pubs."
